WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.300
You know that Doctor Sleep and The Shining
are connected…but how?

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.380
Well, you don't need psychic abilities to
figure that one out: Today we're explaining

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.800
the many connections between the two films,
including returning characters and returning

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:13.800
themes.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:19.490
In The Shining, Stephen King introduced us
to Danny Torrance, a deeply strange little

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.200
boy who has the ability to see ghosts and
communicate telepathically.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.560
"How'd you like some ice cream, Doc?"

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.540
After Danny and his parents move into The
Overlook Hotel for the winter, a host of ghosts

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.660
start slowly or not so slowly driving his
father mad.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.380
They also take a significant toll on Danny.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:48.180
"Redrum, redrum."

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.220
Danny and his mother ultimately manage to
escape the mayhem, but the haunted hotel costs

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.600
Jack Torrance his life.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:58.000
Most of Doctor Sleep focuses on Danny as an
adult.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.920
He now calls himself just Dan, and he finds
that as he gets older, his mysterious "shining"

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:05.720
ability is often too much to bear.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:11.320
Like his father before him, he descends into
alcoholism as a way to numb his gift... but

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.640
the ghosts of the past still manage to catch
up with him.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:19.460
In The Shining, The Overlook Hotel might as
well be a character both in the novel and

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:20.380
in the film version.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.320
This formidable fortress is horrifically alive
with ghosts.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:29.490
Thanks to the malevolent powers lurking within,
The Overlook Hotel manages to claim Danny's

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:33.780
father, Jack Torrance…and it very nearly
claims Danny and his mom Wendy.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.119
In King's original novel, The Overlook Hotel
is destroyed when its faulty boiler explodes.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:43.880
Meanwhile, in Stanley Kubrick's film adaptation
of The Shining, the hotel is left standing.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:48.549
In King's novel Doctor Sleep, the site of
the burned-down Overlook plays an important

00:01:48.549 --> 00:01:53.670
role, but in the film adaptation, the structure
is still there, exactly as it was left in

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.580
the original film.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.840
"They closed it down, and let it rot."

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:02.880
At the end of The Shining, Danny and Wendy
Torrance leave The Overlook behind … but

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.640
that doesn't mean the hotel's ghostly residents
have left them behind.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.040
"Come play with us."

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:16.360
In the novel Doctor Sleep, we learn that ghosts
continue to torment Danny after his ill-fated

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:17.500
stay at The Overlook.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.120
In fact, they follow him and his mother Wendy
to their new apartment, where Danny becomes

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:25.000
so afraid, he refuses to go into the bathroom.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.780
And which ghosts are haunting him?

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:31.780
Well, the dead woman in the bathtub, for one…the
same creep who attacked Danny and terrified

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:32.780
Jack in The Shining.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:37.940
In fact, she's such a powerful presence, her
decomposing corpse leaves behind physical

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:40.660
residue in the bathroom of Danny and Wendy's
apartment.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:45.040
Though she's the most terrifying and persistent
ghost to return from the Overlook, she's not

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.140
the only spirit that follows poor Danny.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.820
"Come play with us.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.900
Forever and ever…"

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.940
The Torrance family wasn't entirely alone
in their fight against The Overlook Hotel's

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.180
supernatural forces.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:02.900
Early on in the story, Danny is befriended
by the Overlook's cook, Dick Hallorann, who

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.800
reveals to Danny that they both have telepathic
abilities.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.980
Actually, he kind of brags about it.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:13.880
"My grandmother and I could hold conversations
entirely without ever opening our mouths."

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:19.240
But King's book and Kubrick's movie go in
two very different directions.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.840
Dick winds up brutally killed in the movie,
but he survives in the novel.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:27.840
In fact, he remains friends with Wendy and
Danny Torrance after they manage to escape

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.460
the hotel.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:33.180
Dick also pops up in Doctor Sleep both in
the novel and in the movie.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:38.140
The character played by the late Scatman Crothers
in The Shining is now played by Carl Lumbly.

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:42.540
When Danny has difficulty shaking off the
ghosts of the Overlook, Dick pays him a visit

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:44.840
and helps him to compartmentalize his trauma.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:49.100
Even after Dick dies, he isn't entirely gone
from Dan Torrance's life.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.640
That's the shining for you.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:56.280
Without question, the bond that forms between
Danny Torrance and Dick Hallorann is one of

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.280
the most important relationships in The Shining.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:03.160
In fact, their psychic connection is so strong,
it allows Danny to telepathically contact

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.120
Dick from halfway across the country.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:10.600
In Doctor Sleep, Dan develops a new psychic
connection with a young girl named Abra Stone.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:15.860
Abra's shining begins to manifest when she's
only a baby, and it's so strong, she manages

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:18.760
to establish a connection with Dan by accident.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:24.340
It's Abra, not Dan, who first discovers the
dark forces at work in Doctor Sleep, and the

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:29.639
two psychics realize they must ultimately
work together to defeat some truly nasty characters.

00:04:29.639 --> 00:04:30.639
"You're magic.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:31.400
Like me."

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.240
"I always called it the Shining."

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.080
The Overlook is essentially the central villain
in The Shining.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:41.440
The hotel's supernatural powers prey on the
Torrance family, threatening to drive them

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:42.920
insane... or worse.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:47.630
But in Doctor Sleep, the main villains are
a group of psychic vampires called The True

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:48.220
Knot.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:49.700
Who are these jerks?

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:54.300
Well...they're a forceful group of immoral
nomads who prolong their lives by feeding

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.480
off the essence of people who can shine.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:01.520
They're led by a devious figure known as Rose
the Hat, who chooses the Knot's victims and

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:03.040
finds new members to initiate.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:06.460
"You are a special little thing, aren't you?"

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:11.160
When The True Knot become aware of Abra, they
hatch a plan to track her down and consume

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:12.360
all of her psychic gifts.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:16.780
In the novel Doctor Sleep, we learn that The
True Knot has a rather strange connection

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:17.920
to The Overlook Hotel.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.920
As Stephen King writes in Doctor Sleep,

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:26.260
"The True’s towns, with colorful names like
Dry Bend, Jerusalem’s Lot, Oree, and Sidewinder,

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:31.180
were safe havens, but they never stayed in
those places for long; mostly they were migratory."

00:05:31.389 --> 00:05:33.180
So what's the connection, exactly?

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:37.120
Well, in the first chapter of King's novel
The Shining, we learn that

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:40.960
"The Overlook was built in the years 1907
to 1909.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:44.800
The closest town is Sidewinder, forty miles
east."

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:50.580
This means The True Knot is inextricably tied
to the haunted hotel that changed Dan Torrance's

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:51.540
life forever.

